---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Link from "../../components/Link.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Autowealth + CompoundFox — Algo trading platform with live dashboard | Alejandro Martínez"
  description="Built CompoundFox algorithmic trading strategy with a live, public performance dashboard. Full equity curve, Sharpe and drawdown updated in real time. Autowealth is the SaaS distribution layer: Turborepo monorepo with backend, Telegram bot, Next dashboards, React Native, and AWS CDK."
>
  <div class="page"> 

    <!-- top bar -->
    <header class="topbar">
      <Brand />
      <nav class="topbar-nav">
        <Link href="/">← back</Link>
        <Link href="/#case-studies">case studies</Link>
        <Link href="mailto:alex@konar.es">contact</Link>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- hero -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-tag">CASE STUDY · 06</div>
        <div class="hero-main">
          <div class="hero-meta">ALGORITHMIC TRADING · DISTRIBUTION PLATFORM &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2024 — now &nbsp;·&nbsp; SOLE ENGINEER</div>
          <h1 class="hero-h1">CompoundFox strategy with a live, public performance dashboard.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Autowealth is a SaaS distribution platform for algorithmic trading strategies. CompoundFox
            is the flagship strategy — full equity curve, Sharpe ratio and drawdown updated in real time
            on a public dashboard. The platform includes a Turborepo monorepo with backend, Telegram bot,
            Next.js dashboards, React Native mobile app, and AWS CDK infrastructure.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <div class="hero-links-label">LINKS</div>
          <Link href="https://autowealth.trade" class="hero-link">autowealth.trade ↗</Link>
          <Link href="https://stats.autowealth.trade" class="hero-link">stats.autowealth.trade ↗</Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- numbers strip -->
    <div class="numbers">
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">STRATEGY</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">CompoundFox</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">flagship algorithm</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">DASHBOARD</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">live</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">equity curve · sharpe · drawdown</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">PLATFORM</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">SaaS</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">distribution layer for strategies</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">MONOREPO</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">Turborepo</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">backend · bot · dashboards · mobile</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">INFRA</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">AWS</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">CDK · ECS · CloudWatch</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell numbers-cell--last">
        <div class="numbers-key">STRATEGIES</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">3+</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">CompoundFox · AlgoAI · Forex</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- the brief -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="THE BRIEF" title="A trading strategy with proof.">
      <p class="body-para">
        Most algo strategies are sold on backtests. Autowealth publishes live performance: full equity
        curve, Sharpe and drawdown, updated in real time, publicly accessible before anyone commits
        capital. CompoundFox is the flagship — running live on Bybit since 2024. The platform is
        built as a distribution layer for multiple strategies, not a single-strategy product.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- architecture -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="ARCHITECTURE" title="Turborepo monorepo: backend, bot, dashboards, mobile.">
      <pre class="arch-diagram">  ┌─ Turborepo monorepo
  │
  ├── apps/
  │   ├── backend              [ Bun · TypeScript · Jesse (backtesting) ]
  │   │      Bybit API integration · trade execution · performance calculation
  │   │
  │   ├── telegram-bot         [ Telegraf · TypeScript ]
  │   │      strategy signals · performance alerts · follower management
  │   │
  │   ├── dashboard            [ Next.js 14 · React Query · shadcn/ui ]
  │   │      live equity curve · Sharpe · drawdown · real-time metrics
  │   │
  │   └── mobile               [ React Native ]
  │          strategy overview · performance charts · notifications
  │
  └── infra/
       └── aws-cdk             [ TypeScript · ECS · CloudWatch · RDS ]
              auto-scaling · monitoring · blue/green deploys
</pre>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- decisions -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="DECISIONS" title="Four calls that define the platform.">
      <div class="decisions-grid">
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">01 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Live public dashboard over periodic reports</div>
          <p class="decision-body">No email reports, no cherry-picked screenshots. The dashboard is a live feed: equity curve, Sharpe, drawdown, all pulled from the running engine. Anyone can check it before subscribing. Publishing in real time removes the option of curating what gets shown.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">02 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Turborepo monorepo over separate repos</div>
          <p class="decision-body">The backend, Telegram bot, dashboard and mobile app share performance calculations, API client types and constants. With four apps that must agree on what a "trade" or "drawdown" means, a monorepo isn't a preference — it's the only way to keep them from drifting. Turborepo handles incremental builds and the shared deployment pipeline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">03 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Strategy-agnostic distribution layer</div>
          <p class="decision-body">CompoundFox is the first strategy, but the platform is not built around it. Each strategy gets its own performance tracking, risk metrics and follower management — the distribution infrastructure is shared. Adding AlgoAI or Forex doesn't touch the platform; it adds a config and a data source.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">04 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Bybit as primary exchange</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Bybit's WebSocket API is stable enough to build a copy trading system on top of, and its REST endpoints handle trade execution without the rate-limit issues that make Binance harder to use as a master. Copy Trader (the engine behind Autowealth) also handles Binance and Hyperliquid as follower exchanges — but the master feed is Bybit only.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ownership -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OWNERSHIP" title="The full stack: backend, bot, dashboards, mobile, infra.">
      <div class="ownership-scroll"><div class="ownership">
        <div class="ownership-header">
          <span>COMPONENT</span>
          <span>STACK</span>
          <span class="text-right">ROLE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Trading backend</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">bun · typescript · jesse · bybit api</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Performance engine</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">equity curve · sharpe · drawdown · real-time</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Next.js dashboard</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">next.js 14 · react query · shadcn/ui</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">Telegram bot</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">telegraf · typescript · strategy signals</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">React Native mobile</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">react native · performance charts · notifications</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">AWS infrastructure</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">typescript · aws cdk · ecs · cloudwatch</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
      </div></div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- outcome -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OUTCOME" title="A production trading platform with real-time transparency.">
      <p class="body-para">
        CompoundFox has been running live since 2024 with a Sharpe of 5.26 and +56% ROI over 137
        days on a public dashboard anyone can verify. That's the point: the performance is either
        defensible or it isn't. Autowealth as the distribution layer is working — the harder part
        was building a copy trading engine (Copy Trader) that handles three exchanges, per-follower
        position math, and real-money idempotency without a margin for error.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- next case -->
    <div class="next-case">
      <span class="next-case-label">NEXT CASE STUDY</span>
      <Link href="/cases/copy-trader" class="next-case-link">
        07 &nbsp; Copy Trader — Multi-exchange copy trading engine →
      </Link>
    </div>

    <!-- footer -->
    <footer class="footer">
      <span>alejandro martinez · @lyricalstring · oss under konar technologies</span>
      <span>alex@konar.es</span>
    </footer>

  </div>

</Base>


<style>
  @import "../../styles/case-study.css";

  /* ── OWNERSHIP TABLE: autowealth has 3 columns (2fr 2fr 1fr) ── */
  .ownership-header,
  .ownership-row {
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 2fr 1fr;
  }

  /* hover effect on next-case-link (under hover:hover for touch safety) */
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .next-case-link:hover {
      color: var(--accent);
    }
  }
</style>
